Description: Remove buggy deb_build_arch self-assignment in gcc_toolchain.gni
 The Debian Chromium 143 cross-build.patch adds a buggy line that attempts to
 suppress GN's "Assignment had no effect" warning by self-assigning deb_build_arch.
 However, this line is unnecessary because deb_build_arch is already defined by
 getenv() on line 798 and is used correctly inside toolchain_args on line 822.
 The self-assignment causes either "Assignment had no effect" (when env var is empty)
 or "Undefined identifier" (depending on GN version). Simply remove the buggy lines.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-12

diff --git a/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni b/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
index 9285ec8..f2b9a62 100644
--- a/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
+++ b/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
@@ -801,9 +801,6 @@ template("gcc_rust_host_build_tools_toolchain") {
     #cxx           = getenv("RUST_MACRO_CXX")
     extra_ldflags  = getenv("RUST_MACRO_LDFLAGS")

-    # Avoid "Assignment had no effect" error when env var is unset
-    deb_build_arch = deb_build_arch
-
     toolchain_args = {
       # Populate toolchain args from the invoker.
       forward_variables_from(invoker.toolchain_args, "*")
